course: dictionary
lesson: 4989
title: Words that do not care
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «He seemed indifferent to the danger» means he did not care about it. Ask yourself: is the sentence about feelings or interest? If it is, the meaning is probably "does not care".
explain: Indifferent can also mean ordinary, or rather poor. «The food was indifferent» means the food was only ordinary, not very good. Look at what the sentence is describing: a meal, a player, a performance. Those are things that can be good or bad, so the word is talking about quality.
explain: Look for the word "to" nearby. Indifferent is often followed by "to", as in «indifferent to the cold», which tells you the cold does not bother the person. When you see "indifferent to", think "does not care about".
fact: Indifferent means not caring about something, or not being interested in it.
fact: Indifferent can also mean only ordinary, or rather poor: «an indifferent meal».
fact: Indifferently is the adverb, meaning in an indifferent way.
fact: Indifferent is often followed by «to», as in «indifferent to the cold».
fact: The sentence «The wood holds good, bad, and indifferent» uses indifferent as the middle point of a list, between good and bad.
exercise: «He seemed indifferent to the danger.» What does indifferent mean here? | *He did not care about the danger | He wanted to warn everyone | He was terrified of the danger | He was lost in the woods
exercise: «The food was indifferent.» What does indifferent mean in this review? | Delicious and very rare | *Not very good, only ordinary | Cold and wet | Given out for free
exercise: Complete the phrase: «indifferent ___ the cold», meaning the cold does not bother her. | about | *to | from | with
test: «The wood holds good, bad, and indifferent.» In this list, indifferent means | Very loud | Better than good | Hidden among the trees | *Ordinary or rather poor
test: Which sentence shows indifferent meaning does not care? | The bread was indifferent. | The room was indifferent. | The film was indifferent. | *He was indifferent to the cheers.
exam: Ruby reads «the team gave an indifferent performance». What does indifferent mean? | Brilliant and famous | *Only ordinary, not very good | Wild and noisy | Sad and tired
